    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b0a2ee05-c6ad-5c39-80c7-d95c47e9e438",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z &=-1 \\\\ x+2y-z &=3 \\\\ x+3z &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & -5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1){R}_{2} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. Here there is one free variable, $z$. Therefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, select: The system is consistent dependent.",
