    "question": {
      ":question/id": "cd3abac3-856b-50b3-926b-46303a552a34",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y+2z &=-3 \\\\ -x-2y-3z &=0 \\\\ -2x-4y-6z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -4 & -6 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -4 & -6 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(1){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -4 & -6 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y+0z=3,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, select: The system is inconsistent.",
